grainworks.tech
a manifesto

the machine is already running.

data centers hum whether you're logged on or not. models have been trained on data stolen from all of humanity. compute is being burned on slop. this isn't whether we use ai but what for.

we acknowledge the contradiction. ai's environmental cost is real. its corporate capture is entrenched. technology connects our data to shareholder dividends, not to our paychecks. 

and so, the cat is out of the bag. you are already in the machine. the question is whether you're running it or being run. and retreating to a private bunker is not an option for us. 

so what do we actually do with it?

do we replace the creative process? the struggles that humans endure in pursuit of growth? no, we need tools that claw back time, attention, and agency from tech run amok. not optimization for its own sake.

grainworks is a research lab exploring ai that treats you like a person, not a pattern. we dream, build, and test things that let you get back to living. wood, steel, electrons, and lines of code are all the same thing to us. we're building with the same materials that built the cage. we don't pretend otherwise. we're just trying to make a tool instead of a trap.

why can't ai do your laundry? who profits from what it learns? what happens if you refuse to play?

we are working to find out.

most technology is designed to need you. we're interested in technology that you need.

as we sand and treat wood, so we work with the grain of humanity.

things that help people organize, understand, repair, connect, and grow... without selling their data or dignity.

this is not a professional blog... this is not thought leadership. this is a workshop. we're offering something that might break, might fail, might only work for you. that's the point.

the machines are running. let's make it worth it.

